\sectionScored{Meal reservation contribution}{C1-\sml{3}}{sec:q1}

A meal vendor handles three meal reservations. Each reservation independently has exactly two mutually exclusive possible outcomes: the buyer keeps it with probability 0.4, or cancels it with probability 0.6. These probabilities apply to every reservation. Each kept reservation contributes 7 USD and each cancellation contributes no money. A fixed handling cost of 5 USD is then deducted once from the combined contribution. There are no other receipts or costs. Record the net contribution for the three meal reservations.

\Needspace{8\baselineskip}
\subsection*{Task 1 --- question and worked solution (proposed allocation) \score{1}}
\label{sol:q1t1}

\noindent\textbf{\boldmath List every complete outcome in order and calculate its probability.}\par\nopagebreak

Write $\GTenHLOutcome{K}$ for \GTenHLOutcome{kept} and $\GTenHLOutcome{C}$ for \GTenHLOutcome{cancelled}. There are $2^{3}=8$ ordered complete outcomes. Independence permits multiplication within each triple; it does not make the triples equally likely.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{ccc}\toprule
Ordered outcome & Product & Exact probability\\\midrule
$\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{KKK}}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.4}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{8/125}=\GTenHLProbability{0.064}$\\
$\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{KKC}}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.4}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.6}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{12/125}=\GTenHLProbability{0.096}$\\
$\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{KCK}}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.4}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.6}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{12/125}=\GTenHLProbability{0.096}$\\
$\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{KCC}}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.4}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.6}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.6}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{18/125}=\GTenHLProbability{0.144}$\\
$\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{CKK}}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.6}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{12/125}=\GTenHLProbability{0.096}$\\
$\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{CKC}}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.6}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.6}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{18/125}=\GTenHLProbability{0.144}$\\
$\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{CCK}}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.6}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.6}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{18/125}=\GTenHLProbability{0.144}$\\
$\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{CCC}}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.6}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.6}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.6}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{27/125}=\GTenHLProbability{0.216}$\\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}
\end{center}

The eight probabilities sum to $(\GTenHLProbability{2/5}+\GTenHLProbability{3/5})^{3}=\GTenHLProbability{1}$.

\par\smallskip
\noindent\begin{minipage}{\linewidth}\centering
\textbf{Proposed partial credit.}\par\smallskip
\begin{tabular}{@{}l r@{}}\toprule
\CreditDescription{\textbf{Assessed step or criterion}} & \textbf{Points}\\\midrule
\CreditDescription{All eight ordered outcomes} & 0.5\\
\CreditDescription{Their probabilities using independent products} & 0.5\\
\midrule
\CreditDescription{\textbf{Total}} & \textbf{1}\\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}
\end{minipage}\par\smallskip

\par\vspace{3mm}\secInicio[][sec:q1]

\Needspace{8\baselineskip}
\subsection*{Task 2 --- question and worked solution (proposed allocation) \score{1}}
\label{sol:q1t2}

\noindent\textbf{\boldmath Define the random variable and its units. Map every complete outcome to a value, identify the support, and construct the grouped PMF.}\par\nopagebreak

Let $\GTenHLValue{X}$ be the \GTenHLValue{net contribution} from the three meal reservations, in \GTenHLValue{USD}. If $\GTenHLSecond{N}$ is the number kept, $\GTenHLValue{X}=\GTenHLValue{7}\GTenHLSecond{N}-\GTenHLValue{5}$. The table maps all eight outcomes and groups those with the same \GTenHLValue{net contribution}.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{ccc}\toprule
$\GTenHLValue{x}$ (\GTenHLValue{USD}) & Complete outcomes & Grouped probability\\\midrule
$-\GTenHLValue{5}$ & $\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{CCC}}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{27/125}=\GTenHLProbability{27/125}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{2}$ & $\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{KCC}},\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{CKC}},\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{CCK}}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{18/125}+\GTenHLProbability{18/125}+\GTenHLProbability{18/125}=\GTenHLProbability{54/125}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{9}$ & $\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{KKC}},\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{KCK}},\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{CKK}}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{12/125}+\GTenHLProbability{12/125}+\GTenHLProbability{12/125}=\GTenHLProbability{36/125}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{16}$ & $\GTenHLOutcome{\mathrm{KKK}}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{8/125}=\GTenHLProbability{8/125}$\\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}
\end{center}

Thus $\GTenHLValue{S_X}=\{-\GTenHLValue{5},\GTenHLValue{2},\GTenHLValue{9},\GTenHLValue{16}\}$ \GTenHLValue{USD}. The \GTenHLProbability{PMF} is the last column.
\Needspace{5\baselineskip}\textbf{PMF checks.}
\begin{itemize}
\item Nonnegativity: all listed masses are positive.
\item Normalization: $(\GTenHLProbability{27}+\GTenHLProbability{54}+\GTenHLProbability{36}+\GTenHLProbability{8})/\GTenHLProbability{125}=\GTenHLProbability{1}$.
\item Outside the \GTenHLValue{support}: the \GTenHLProbability{PMF} is zero elsewhere.
\end{itemize}

A negative value means the handling cost exceeds receipts.

\par\smallskip
\noindent\begin{minipage}{\linewidth}\centering
\textbf{Proposed partial credit.}\par\smallskip
\begin{tabular}{@{}l r@{}}\toprule
\CreditDescription{\textbf{Assessed step or criterion}} & \textbf{Points}\\\midrule
\CreditDescription{The variable and units} & 0.125\\
\CreditDescription{All outcome mappings} & 0.25\\
\CreditDescription{Support} & 0.125\\
\CreditDescription{Grouped PMF masses} & 0.375\\
\CreditDescription{Positivity and normalization checks} & 0.125\\
\midrule
\CreditDescription{\textbf{Total}} & \textbf{1}\\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}
\end{minipage}\par\smallskip

\par\vspace{3mm}\secInicio[][sec:q1]

\Needspace{8\baselineskip}
\subsection*{Task 3 --- question and worked solution (proposed allocation) \score{1}}
\label{sol:q1t3}

\noindent\textbf{\boldmath Calculate and interpret the probability that the net contribution is exactly 9 USD.}\par\nopagebreak

From the grouped \GTenHLProbability{PMF}, $P(\GTenHLValue{X}=\GTenHLValue{9})=\GTenHLProbability{p_X(9)}=\GTenHLProbability{36/125}=\GTenHLProbability{0.288}=\GTenHLProbability{28.8\%}$. The vendor earns a \GTenHLValue{net contribution} of exactly \GTenHLValue{9 USD} with probability \GTenHLProbability{28.8\%}; this happens exactly when two reservations are kept and one is cancelled.

\par\smallskip
\noindent\begin{minipage}{\linewidth}\centering
\textbf{Proposed partial credit.}\par\smallskip
\begin{tabular}{@{}l r@{}}\toprule
\CreditDescription{\textbf{Assessed step or criterion}} & \textbf{Points}\\\midrule
\CreditDescription{Selecting the correct mass at $X=9$} & 0.5\\
\CreditDescription{The contextual interpretation} & 0.5\\
\midrule
\CreditDescription{\textbf{Total}} & \textbf{1}\\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}
\end{minipage}\par\smallskip

Question total: 3 points for C1.

\par\vspace{3mm}\secInicio[][sec:q1]

\clearpage
\sectionScored{Two distributor promotional credits}{C1-\sml{3}}{sec:q2}

A bookshop receives one promotional credit from each of two distributors. The distributors award credits independently. Each has exactly three mutually exclusive possible outcomes: no credit, a 4 USD credit, or a 9 USD credit. For the first distributor these probabilities are 0.2, 0.5 and 0.3, respectively. For the second distributor they are 0.4, 0.4 and 0.2, respectively. Add both credits; there are no other adjustments. Record the total credit, keeping first-distributor then second-distributor order.

\Needspace{8\baselineskip}
\subsection*{Task 1 --- question and worked solution (proposed allocation) \score{1}}
\label{sol:q2t1}

\noindent\textbf{\boldmath List every complete ordered outcome and calculate its probability.}\par\nopagebreak

Each distributor has three possible outcomes, giving $3^{2}=9$ ordered pairs. Write a pair as its two credit amounts, in \GTenHLValue{USD}. Multiply the appropriate probabilities by independence.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{ccc}\toprule
Ordered credit outcome (\GTenHLValue{USD}) & Product & Exact probability\\\midrule
$(\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{0})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.2}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{2/25}=\GTenHLProbability{0.08}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{4})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.2}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{2/25}=\GTenHLProbability{0.08}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{9})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.2}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.2}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{1/25}=\GTenHLProbability{0.04}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{4},\GTenHLOutcome{0})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.5}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{1/5}=\GTenHLProbability{0.20}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{4},\GTenHLOutcome{4})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.5}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{1/5}=\GTenHLProbability{0.20}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{4},\GTenHLOutcome{9})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.5}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.2}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{1/10}=\GTenHLProbability{0.10}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{9},\GTenHLOutcome{0})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.3}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{3/25}=\GTenHLProbability{0.12}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{9},\GTenHLOutcome{4})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.3}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.4}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{3/25}=\GTenHLProbability{0.12}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{9},\GTenHLOutcome{9})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{0.3}\cdot\GTenHLProbability{0.2}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{3/50}=\GTenHLProbability{0.06}$\\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}
\end{center}

Exhaustiveness check: $(\GTenHLProbability{0.2}+\GTenHLProbability{0.5}+\GTenHLProbability{0.3})(\GTenHLProbability{0.4}+\GTenHLProbability{0.4}+\GTenHLProbability{0.2})=\GTenHLProbability{1}$.

\par\smallskip
\noindent\begin{minipage}{\linewidth}\centering
\textbf{Proposed partial credit.}\par\smallskip
\begin{tabular}{@{}l r@{}}\toprule
\CreditDescription{\textbf{Assessed step or criterion}} & \textbf{Points}\\\midrule
\CreditDescription{All nine ordered pairs} & 0.5\\
\CreditDescription{Independent product probabilities} & 0.5\\
\midrule
\CreditDescription{\textbf{Total}} & \textbf{1}\\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}
\end{minipage}\par\smallskip

\par\vspace{3mm}\secInicio[][sec:q2]

\Needspace{8\baselineskip}
\subsection*{Task 2 --- question and worked solution (proposed allocation) \score{1}}
\label{sol:q2t2}

\noindent\textbf{\boldmath Define the random variable and units; map every outcome to a value; identify the support; construct the grouped PMF.}\par\nopagebreak

Let $\GTenHLValue{X}$ be the \GTenHLValue{total promotional credit} from the two distributors, in \GTenHLValue{USD}. Add the two amounts in each pair. The complete mapping and grouped \GTenHLProbability{PMF} are:

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{ccc}\toprule
$\GTenHLValue{x}$ (\GTenHLValue{USD}) & Ordered outcomes & Grouped probability\\\midrule
$\GTenHLValue{0}$ & $(\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{0})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{2/25}=\GTenHLProbability{2/25}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{4}$ & $(\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{4}),(\GTenHLOutcome{4},\GTenHLOutcome{0})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{2/25}+\GTenHLProbability{1/5}=\GTenHLProbability{7/25}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{8}$ & $(\GTenHLOutcome{4},\GTenHLOutcome{4})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{1/5}=\GTenHLProbability{1/5}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{9}$ & $(\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{9}),(\GTenHLOutcome{9},\GTenHLOutcome{0})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{1/25}+\GTenHLProbability{3/25}=\GTenHLProbability{4/25}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{13}$ & $(\GTenHLOutcome{4},\GTenHLOutcome{9}),(\GTenHLOutcome{9},\GTenHLOutcome{4})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{1/10}+\GTenHLProbability{3/25}=\GTenHLProbability{11/50}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{18}$ & $(\GTenHLOutcome{9},\GTenHLOutcome{9})$ & $\GTenHLProbability{3/50}=\GTenHLProbability{3/50}$\\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}
\end{center}

The \GTenHLValue{support} is $\GTenHLValue{S_X}=\{\GTenHLValue{0},\GTenHLValue{4},\GTenHLValue{8},\GTenHLValue{9},\GTenHLValue{13},\GTenHLValue{18}\}$ \GTenHLValue{USD}, with the grouped masses shown above.
\Needspace{5\baselineskip}\textbf{PMF checks.}
\begin{itemize}
\item Nonnegativity: all listed masses are positive.
\item Normalization: $(\GTenHLProbability{4}+\GTenHLProbability{14}+\GTenHLProbability{10}+\GTenHLProbability{8}+\GTenHLProbability{11}+\GTenHLProbability{3})/\GTenHLProbability{50}=\GTenHLProbability{50/50}=\GTenHLProbability{1}$.
\item Outside the \GTenHLValue{support}: the \GTenHLProbability{PMF} has zero mass elsewhere.
\end{itemize}

Reversing a pair can preserve its monetary value while changing its probability.

\par\smallskip
\noindent\begin{minipage}{\linewidth}\centering
\textbf{Proposed partial credit.}\par\smallskip
\begin{tabular}{@{}l r@{}}\toprule
\CreditDescription{\textbf{Assessed step or criterion}} & \textbf{Points}\\\midrule
\CreditDescription{Variable and units} & 0.125\\
\CreditDescription{All mappings} & 0.25\\
\CreditDescription{Support} & 0.125\\
\CreditDescription{Grouped masses} & 0.375\\
\CreditDescription{Positivity and normalization checks} & 0.125\\
\midrule
\CreditDescription{\textbf{Total}} & \textbf{1}\\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}
\end{minipage}\par\smallskip

\par\vspace{3mm}\secInicio[][sec:q2]

\Needspace{8\baselineskip}
\subsection*{Task 3 --- question and worked solution (proposed allocation) \score{1}}
\label{sol:q2t3}

\noindent\textbf{\boldmath Calculate and interpret the probability that the total credit is exactly 13 USD.}\par\nopagebreak

$P(\GTenHLValue{X}=\GTenHLValue{13})=\GTenHLProbability{p_X(13)}=\GTenHLProbability{11/50}=\GTenHLProbability{0.22}=\GTenHLProbability{22\%}$. The bookshop receives a total credit of exactly \GTenHLValue{13 USD} with probability \GTenHLProbability{22\%}; the qualifying pairs are $(\GTenHLValue{4},\GTenHLValue{9})$ and $(\GTenHLValue{9},\GTenHLValue{4})$.

\par\smallskip
\noindent\begin{minipage}{\linewidth}\centering
\textbf{Proposed partial credit.}\par\smallskip
\begin{tabular}{@{}l r@{}}\toprule
\CreditDescription{\textbf{Assessed step or criterion}} & \textbf{Points}\\\midrule
\CreditDescription{Selecting the correct mass at $X=13$} & 0.5\\
\CreditDescription{The contextual interpretation} & 0.5\\
\midrule
\CreditDescription{\textbf{Total}} & \textbf{1}\\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}
\end{minipage}\par\smallskip

Question total: 3 points for C1. Criterion C1 total: 6 points; independent pass: at least 4 points.

\par\vspace{3mm}\secInicio[][sec:q2]

