\sectionScored{Produce crate delivery fees}{C2-\sml{2}}{sec:q3}

A farm cooperative sends one produce crate using exactly one of eight exhaustive, mutually exclusive delivery methods: walking courier, bicycle, cargo bicycle, motorcycle, car, van, refrigerated van or truck. Their probabilities are 0.10, 0.10, 0.15, 0.20, 0.15, 0.10, 0.10 and 0.10, respectively. The corresponding fixed handling fees are 0, 0, 3, 6, 10, 15, 21 and 29 USD, respectively. No other handling charges apply. Record the handling fee for the crate.

\Needspace{8\baselineskip}
\subsection*{Task 1 --- question and worked solution (proposed allocation) \score{0.5}}
\label{sol:q3t1}

\noindent\textbf{\boldmath Define the random variable and support; derive the grouped PMF; produce its table and a labeled graph with actual monetary spacing.}\par\nopagebreak

Let $\GTenHLValue{X}$ be the \GTenHLValue{handling fee} for one produce crate, in \GTenHLValue{USD}. Map the supplied categories to payments:

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{ccc}\toprule
Category & Given probability & $\GTenHLValue{X}$ (\GTenHLValue{USD})\\\midrule
\GTenHLOutcome{Walking courier} & $\GTenHLProbability{0.10}=\GTenHLProbability{2/20}$ & $\GTenHLValue{0}$\\
\GTenHLOutcome{Bicycle} & $\GTenHLProbability{0.10}=\GTenHLProbability{2/20}$ & $\GTenHLValue{0}$\\
\GTenHLOutcome{Cargo bicycle} & $\GTenHLProbability{0.15}=\GTenHLProbability{3/20}$ & $\GTenHLValue{3}$\\
\GTenHLOutcome{Motorcycle} & $\GTenHLProbability{0.20}=\GTenHLProbability{4/20}$ & $\GTenHLValue{6}$\\
\GTenHLOutcome{Car} & $\GTenHLProbability{0.15}=\GTenHLProbability{3/20}$ & $\GTenHLValue{10}$\\
\GTenHLOutcome{Van} & $\GTenHLProbability{0.10}=\GTenHLProbability{2/20}$ & $\GTenHLValue{15}$\\
\GTenHLOutcome{Refrigerated van} & $\GTenHLProbability{0.10}=\GTenHLProbability{2/20}$ & $\GTenHLValue{21}$\\
\GTenHLOutcome{Truck} & $\GTenHLProbability{0.10}=\GTenHLProbability{2/20}$ & $\GTenHLValue{29}$\\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}
\end{center}

The walking courier and bicycle are distinct outcomes sharing a zero fee, so $\GTenHLProbability{p_X(0)}=\GTenHLProbability{0.10}+\GTenHLProbability{0.10}=\GTenHLProbability{0.20}=\GTenHLProbability{4/20}$. Every other method has its own fee and retains its supplied probability.

$\GTenHLValue{S_X}=\{\GTenHLValue{0},\GTenHLValue{3},\GTenHLValue{6},\GTenHLValue{10},\GTenHLValue{15},\GTenHLValue{21},\GTenHLValue{29}\}$ \GTenHLValue{USD}. There are eight elementary outcomes but seven distinct monetary values. Add probabilities of mutually exclusive categories sharing a value, because the events cannot occur together.

\begin{center}
\begin{minipage}{.26\linewidth}\centering
\begin{tabular}{cc}\toprule
$\GTenHLValue{x}$ (\GTenHLValue{USD}) & $\GTenHLProbability{p_X(x)}$\\\midrule
$\GTenHLValue{0}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{4/20}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{3}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{3/20}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{6}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{4/20}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{10}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{3/20}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{15}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{2/20}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{21}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{2/20}$\\
$\GTenHLValue{29}$ & $\GTenHLProbability{2/20}$\\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}
\end{minipage}\hfill
\begin{minipage}{.70\linewidth}\centering
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[keyaxis,width=.94\linewidth,height=5cm,xmin=-2,xmax=31,ymin=0,ymax=.35,xtick={0,3,6,10,15,21,29},xticklabel style={rotate=45,anchor=north east},ylabel={$\GTenHLProbability{p_X(x)}$},yticklabel={$\GTenHLProbability{\pgfmathprintnumber{\tick}}$},ytick={0,.05,.1,.15,.2,.25,.3}]
\draw[fill=keyMassFill,draw=keyMassColor] (axis cs:-0.45,0) rectangle (axis cs:0.45,4/20);
\draw[fill=keyMassFill,draw=keyMassColor] (axis cs:2.55,0) rectangle (axis cs:3.45,3/20);
