\Needspace{8\baselineskip}
\subsection*{Task 3 (c) --- question and worked solution (proposed allocation) \score{0.5}}
\label{sol:q3t3}

\noindent\textbf{\boldmath Calculate and interpret (i) the probability that the handling fee is less than 10 USD and (ii) the probability that it is at least 21 USD.}\par\nopagebreak

\textbf{Allocation:} (i) 0.25 points; (ii) 0.25 points.

\textbf{(i) Less than \GTenHLValue{10 USD}.} Include only the \GTenHLValue{support} values $\GTenHLValue{0},\GTenHLValue{3},\GTenHLValue{6}$; the mass at \GTenHLValue{10 USD} is excluded because the inequality is strict:
\[
P(\GTenHLValue{X}<\GTenHLValue{10})=\GTenHLProbability{p_X(0)}+\GTenHLProbability{p_X(3)}+\GTenHLProbability{p_X(6)}
=\frac{\GTenHLProbability{4}+\GTenHLProbability{3}+\GTenHLProbability{4}}{\GTenHLProbability{20}}=\GTenHLProbability{\frac{11}{20}}=\GTenHLProbability{0.55}.
\]
The cooperative pays a \GTenHLValue{handling fee} below \GTenHLValue{10 USD} for a crate with probability $\GTenHLProbability{55\%}$.

\textbf{(ii) At least \GTenHLValue{21 USD}.} Include both $\GTenHLValue{21}$ and $\GTenHLValue{29}$; the boundary mass at \GTenHLValue{21 USD} is included:
\[
P(\GTenHLValue{X}\geq\GTenHLValue{21})=\GTenHLProbability{p_X(21)}+\GTenHLProbability{p_X(29)}=\frac{\GTenHLProbability{2}+\GTenHLProbability{2}}{\GTenHLProbability{20}}=\GTenHLProbability{\frac15}=\GTenHLProbability{0.20}.
\]
The cooperative pays a \GTenHLValue{handling fee} of \GTenHLValue{21 USD} or more for a crate with probability $\GTenHLProbability{20\%}$.

