\clearpage
\sectionScored{Library fundraiser prize tickets}{C2-\sml{6}}{sec:q6}

A library fundraiser has nine physically distinct prize tickets: four worth 0 USD each, three worth 6 USD each and two worth 14 USD each. Choose a subset of three tickets uniformly without replacement, so every subset of three physically distinct tickets has the same chance. Ignore selection order. First add the face values. Then add one bonus of 8 USD if the selected subset contains at least one 6 USD ticket and at least one 14 USD ticket; otherwise add no bonus. Finally, if this adjusted amount exceeds 30 USD, pay only 30 USD; otherwise pay the adjusted amount. No other payments or deductions apply. Record the final payout.

\Needspace{8\baselineskip}
\subsection*{Task 1 --- question and worked solution (proposed allocation) \score{1.5}}
\label{sol:q6t1}

\noindent\textbf{\boldmath Define the random variable and support. Count the distinct-ticket selections, apply the bonus and then the cap, aggregate equal final payouts, and derive the PMF. Produce its table and labeled graph.}\par\nopagebreak

Let $\GTenHLValue{X}$ be the \GTenHLValue{final payout} for one three-ticket subset, in \GTenHLValue{USD}. Label the physical tickets $\GTenHLOutcome{Z_1},\ldots,\GTenHLOutcome{Z_4}$, $\GTenHLOutcome{L_1},\ldots,\GTenHLOutcome{L_3}$, and $\GTenHLOutcome{H_1},\GTenHLOutcome{H_2}$, with values 0, 6 and \GTenHLValue{14 USD}. There are
\[
\binom{9}{3}=\frac{9\cdot8\cdot7}{3\cdot2\cdot1}=84
\]
equally likely unordered subsets, each with probability $\GTenHLProbability{1/84}$. A composition records $(a,b,c)$, the counts of zero-, six- and fourteen-dollar tickets. Feasible counts satisfy $a+b+c=3$, $0\leq a\leq4$, $0\leq b\leq3$, and $0\leq c\leq2$. The number of subsets with that composition is
\[
\GTenHLSecond{N}(a,b,c)=\binom{4}{a}\binom{3}{b}\binom{2}{c},\qquad P(a,b,c)=\frac{\GTenHLSecond{N}(a,b,c)}{\GTenHLProbability{84}}.
\]
Define $I=1$ if $b\geq1$ and $c\geq1$, and $I=0$ otherwise. The face sum is $\GTenHLValue{6}b+\GTenHLValue{14}c$; the adjusted amount is $\GTenHLSecond{Y}=\GTenHLValue{6}b+\GTenHLValue{14}c+\GTenHLValue{8}I$; finally $\GTenHLValue{X}=\min\{\GTenHLSecond{Y},\GTenHLValue{30}\}$. The bonus is added once, before the cap.

\begingroup\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.35}

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{ccccccc}\toprule
$(a,b,c)$ & Subset count & Probability & Face sum & Bonus & $\GTenHLSecond{Y}$ & $\GTenHLValue{X}$\\\midrule
$(\GTenHLOutcome{3},\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{0})$ & $\binom4{3}\binom3{0}\binom2{0}=4$ & $\GTenHLProbability{4/84}$ & $\GTenHLValue{0}$ & $\GTenHLValue{0}$ & $\GTenHLSecond{0}$ & $\GTenHLValue{0}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{2},\GTenHLOutcome{1},\GTenHLOutcome{0})$ & $\binom4{2}\binom3{1}\binom2{0}=18$ & $\GTenHLProbability{18/84}$ & $\GTenHLValue{6}$ & $\GTenHLValue{0}$ & $\GTenHLSecond{6}$ & $\GTenHLValue{6}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{1},\GTenHLOutcome{2},\GTenHLOutcome{0})$ & $\binom4{1}\binom3{2}\binom2{0}=12$ & $\GTenHLProbability{12/84}$ & $\GTenHLValue{12}$ & $\GTenHLValue{0}$ & $\GTenHLSecond{12}$ & $\GTenHLValue{12}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{3},\GTenHLOutcome{0})$ & $\binom4{0}\binom3{3}\binom2{0}=1$ & $\GTenHLProbability{1/84}$ & $\GTenHLValue{18}$ & $\GTenHLValue{0}$ & $\GTenHLSecond{18}$ & $\GTenHLValue{18}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{2},\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{1})$ & $\binom4{2}\binom3{0}\binom2{1}=12$ & $\GTenHLProbability{12/84}$ & $\GTenHLValue{14}$ & $\GTenHLValue{0}$ & $\GTenHLSecond{14}$ & $\GTenHLValue{14}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{1},\GTenHLOutcome{1},\GTenHLOutcome{1})$ & $\binom4{1}\binom3{1}\binom2{1}=24$ & $\GTenHLProbability{24/84}$ & $\GTenHLValue{20}$ & $\GTenHLValue{8}$ & $\GTenHLSecond{28}$ & $\GTenHLValue{28}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{2},\GTenHLOutcome{1})$ & $\binom4{0}\binom3{2}\binom2{1}=6$ & $\GTenHLProbability{6/84}$ & $\GTenHLValue{26}$ & $\GTenHLValue{8}$ & $\GTenHLSecond{34}$ & $\GTenHLValue{30}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{1},\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{2})$ & $\binom4{1}\binom3{0}\binom2{2}=4$ & $\GTenHLProbability{4/84}$ & $\GTenHLValue{28}$ & $\GTenHLValue{0}$ & $\GTenHLSecond{28}$ & $\GTenHLValue{28}$\\
$(\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{1},\GTenHLOutcome{2})$ & $\binom4{0}\binom3{1}\binom2{2}=3$ & $\GTenHLProbability{3/84}$ & $\GTenHLValue{34}$ & $\GTenHLValue{8}$ & $\GTenHLSecond{42}$ & $\GTenHLValue{30}$\\
\bottomrule\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\endgroup

All monetary columns are in USD. These nine compositions are exhaustive: list $c=0,1,2$ and every feasible $b$, then $a=3-b-c$. Their counts sum to $4+18+12+1+12+24+6+4+3=84$. Compositions are not equally likely: for example, $(1,1,1)$ represents 24 subsets, whereas $(0,3,0)$ represents only one.

\textbf{Aggregation.} The \GTenHLValue{28 USD} payout comes from $(\GTenHLOutcome{1},\GTenHLOutcome{1},\GTenHLOutcome{1})$ (24 subsets after the bonus) and $(\GTenHLOutcome{1},\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{2})$ (4 subsets without a bonus), so $\GTenHLProbability{p_X(28)}=(\GTenHLProbability{24}+\GTenHLProbability{4})/\GTenHLProbability{84}=\GTenHLProbability{28/84}$. The cap merges the adjusted amounts 34 and \GTenHLValue{42 USD} from $(\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{2},\GTenHLOutcome{1})$ and $(\GTenHLOutcome{0},\GTenHLOutcome{1},\GTenHLOutcome{2})$, so $\GTenHLProbability{p_X(30)}=(\GTenHLProbability{6}+\GTenHLProbability{3})/\GTenHLProbability{84}=\GTenHLProbability{9/84}$. Each other payout arises from one composition.

Thus $\GTenHLValue{S_X}=\{\GTenHLValue{0},\GTenHLValue{6},\GTenHLValue{12},\GTenHLValue{14},\GTenHLValue{18},\GTenHLValue{28},\GTenHLValue{30}\}$ \GTenHLValue{USD}. The cap binds only when the adjusted amount is greater than \GTenHLValue{30 USD}; the \GTenHLValue{28 USD} payout remains unchanged.

