\textbf{CDF checks.}
\begin{itemize}
\item Domain: the table covers every real cutoff.
\item Range: all tabulated heights lie in $[\HLCumulativeProbability{0},\HLCumulativeProbability{1}]$.
\item Monotonicity: the tabulated heights never decrease.
\item Right-continuity: each horizontal segment includes its left endpoint and excludes its right endpoint; the filled point gives the value at a jump.
\item Lower-tail limit: the left arrow extends to $-\infty$, where the limit is 0.
\item Upper-tail limit: the right arrow extends to $+\infty$, where the limit is 1.
\item Jump--mass agreement: in \GTenHLValue{support} order, subtracting successive cumulative numerators (starting at zero) gives $\GTenHLProbability{4},\allowbreak\GTenHLProbability{18},\allowbreak\GTenHLProbability{12},\allowbreak\GTenHLProbability{12},\allowbreak\GTenHLProbability{1},\allowbreak\GTenHLProbability{28},\allowbreak\GTenHLProbability{9}$. Hence each jump is its \GTenHLProbability{PMF} mass over $\GTenHLProbability{84}$: $\HLCumulativeProbability{F_X(a)}-\HLCumulativeProbability{F_X(a^-)}=\GTenHLProbability{p_X(a)}$. At unsupported cutoffs both the jump and the mass are zero.
\end{itemize}

